{"reference":"Micah 2","book":"Micah","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Who Is Speaking?","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verses 6-11 move through commands to stop prophesying, objections, and a prophetic reply. Because the manuscripts do not mark quotation boundaries, interpreters disagree about where one speaker ends and another begins. Reading the exchange as a contested sequence helps account for its abrupt shifts in voice and accusation.","verse_refs":["Micah 2:6-11"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_micah_002_1fd73bf9fc0d445c37cb134c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Land, Dispossession, and Hope","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The opening condemnation concerns powerful people who plan to seize fields, houses, households, and inheritance; the injustice is presented as coercive control over household land. The chapter also names women driven from pleasant homes and children deprived of glory. Its closing promise gathers a remnant and depicts a “breaker” going before them, but the figure’s identity remains disputed: it may be understood as royal, divine, prophetic, or a composite image.","verse_refs":["Micah 2:1-11","Micah 2:1-5","Micah 2:12-13","Micah 2:9"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_micah_002_765d604b0b4e3544852d1d3b"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Micah’s Larger Shape","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"One influential reading of Micah’s final form sees a recurring movement between judgment and hope across chapters 1-2, 3-5, and 6-7. Micah also uses varied forms of speech, including lament, woe, accusation, judgment, and salvation oracles. That broader pattern provides a useful setting for the sharp transition in this chapter from indictment to gathering, though the proposed structure remains debated.","verse_refs":["Micah 1:1-16","Micah 3:1-12","Micah 4:1-13","Micah 5:1-15","Micah 6:1-16","Micah 7:1-20"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_micah_002_ba19187848d82bac822343b1","reader_path_micah_002_ab94ab5914b3b42cb2b48b72"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}